            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-30258",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnupg: verification DoS due to a malicious subkey in the keyring"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In GnuPG before 2.5.5, if a user chooses to import a certificate with certain crafted subkey data that lacks a valid backsig or that has incorrect usage flags, the user loses the ability to verify signatures made from certain other signing keys, aka a \"verification DoS.\""
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-30258",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-30258\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: gpgv\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-30258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-30258)\nIn GnuPG before 2.5.5, if a user chooses to import a certificate with certain crafted subkey data that lacks a valid backsig or that has incorrect usage flags, the user loses the ability to verify signatures made from certain other signing keys, aka a \"verification DoS.\"",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-30258**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|gpgv||[CVE-2025-30258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-30258)|\n\nIn GnuPG before 2.5.5, if a user chooses to import a certificate with certain crafted subkey data that lacks a valid backsig or that has incorrect usage flags, the user loses the ability to verify signatures made from certain other signing keys, aka a \"verification DoS.\""
              },
